<title>USA: U.S. restricts hydrogen sulfide releases at rigs.</title>
<headline>U.S. restricts hydrogen sulfide releases at rigs.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Minerals Management Service said Tuesday it had issued a final rule to prevent hydrogen sulfide releases and step up detection of sulfur dioxide at offshore oil and natural gas operations.</p>
<p>The rule restricts the flaring of hydrogen sulfide, and calls for monitoring and detection of both hydrogen sulfide and sulfur dioxide, which are both toxic.</p>
